    "body": "Shape-mask result on upstream/main `1ae4d061f`. A bridge is narrower than the tab width. This issue goes to `P1`, as its first step says.\n\nThe test reads the material that the posted moves leave under the tab top, on a 0.1 mm grid. The neck of a tab is the widest path through it from the part to the far stock. Tool 6 mm, tab width 4 mm, outside contour, no leads. A plain 40 x 40 part reads 3.89 mm for each of its 4 tabs.\n\n| Case | Distance between the two cuts | Neck of the tab | Note in the output |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| U-turn: a 10 mm notch in the part, a tab on the notch wall | 4 mm | 0.00 mm | none |\n| U-turn: a 14 mm notch | 8 mm | 1.89 mm | none |\n| U-turn: a 20 mm notch | 14 mm | 3.90 mm | none |\n| Second ring: two parts 10 mm apart | 4 mm | 0.00 mm and 0.74 mm | none |\n| Second ring: two parts 14 mm apart | 8 mm | 1.89 mm | none |\n| Second ring: two parts 20 mm apart | 14 mm | 3.89 mm | none |\n\nWhat the readings mean:\n\n- Distance less than the tool diameter: the other cut removes the tab from its stock. The tab holds nothing. This is the `P1` case.\n- Distance between `D` and `W + D`: the tab keeps its width. The stock between the two kerfs is narrower than the tab. That strip has the full cut depth, not only the tab height.\n\nThe test is `crates/motion/tests/contour_tab_necks.rs`. The meter is `crates/motion/tests/common/tab_neck.rs` (`shape_mask.rs` is at 409 lines, so the meter has its own file). The fix follows on branch `issue/2561-tab-bridge-all-cuts`.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
